{"ohhh you mean rasenshuriken huh. its really fun for sure": {"Yassss, the *Wind Release: Repeated Rasenshuriken*? That’s the king of close-range pressure. Two spinning blades, both active at once, slicing through shadows like they’re paper. And when Naruto fires it after Kurama Mode? Yeah, cuts right through the Ten-Tails tail like it’s butter.  \n\nAnd the part where he *meets* the Dragon Blade while fighting Madara? Unstoppable. Like the sky itself cracked open.  \n\nSo yeah, that’s my go-to. Feels like pure instinct. You don’t *think*, you just… *push* the buttons.  \n**Question:** What’s your favorite move in the game that feels like it *comes straight from* the manga/anime? Something that makes you want to scream “YES!” in the middle of a match? 🥋🔥": "invented", "Yass! Exactly, the *Rasenshuriken*? That’s the cherry on top. Double-hit, high-speed spin, and once you’ve got it locked in, it doesn’t just slice, it *resonates*. Feels like the air itself stutters when it hits.  \n\nAnd yeah, after you hit that big ball in the middle of the battlefield? The wind screams and the screen lights up red. Like reality cracked open. That’s the kind of moment you *feel*, not just watch.  \n\nSo tell me, what’s the last match you did? Did you pull off that **Big Ball** move in a tight fight? Or did you use the *Dragon Blade Rasengan* with the emotion spike? That one feels wild, like the ground shook under it. 😏": "skip"}}